# cpptraj script for post-processing Au–thiol SAM trajectory
# Prevents imaging errors and keeps slab fixed in place

parm TEMPO-SAM-11.parm7

# Load trajectories
trajin heat1.nc 1 last 1
trajin equil1.nc 1 last 1
trajin equil1-2.nc 1 last 1
# --- Define atom masks ---
# Au atoms are residues 1–2400
# Linkers are residues 2401–2541
# We exclude hydrogens to avoid noise in fitting

# --- Step 1: Reference frame (slab as origin) ---
# The slab (Au atoms) will remain fixed; we image everything else around it

autoimage anchor :1-2400 origin
autoimage
#   -> First line sets Au atoms as anchor (reference that doesn't move)
#   -> Second line reimages all other atoms relative to this anchor

# --- Step 2: RMS fit (optional) ---
# Fit the system to the gold surface (keeps slab steady)
rms fit :1-2400&!@H= mass

# Alternatively, if you want linkers to appear stationary instead of the slab:
# rms fit :2401-2541&!@H= mass

# --- Step 3: Output cleaned trajectory ---
trajout TEMPO-SAM-11.xtc xtc

run
quit
